│ □ agent-hub's unittest suite needs a short TMPDIR and markdown-it-py on
│   PYTHONPATH; run it with uv, not bare python.
│   + missing  2×  ••  ▾ evidence 2
│
│   <date>      claude ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
│     Hit it again from a worktree: `python -m unittest` failed 20 socket
│     tests with AF_UNIX path too long.
│
│   <date>      pi  migrated ──────────────────────────────────────────────
│     Why the repo didn't say it
│     Both failures look like code errors, and nothing in the repo states
│     the TMPDIR requirement or the markdown-it-py dependency that only the
│     nix build supplies; an agent would report 20 fake failures.
│
│     Details
│     From pkgs/agent-hub: TMPDIR=<tmp>   PYTHONPATH=. uv run --quiet
│     --with markdown-it-py python -m unittest discover -s tests -p
│     'test_*.py'.
│     Without a short TMPDIR the socket tests fail with "OSError: AF_UNIX
│     path too long" inside a long worktree path; without markdown-it-py
│     the render/features imports fail.
│     Baseline: 470 tests, 1 skipped.
│
